From: Devesh Rai <devesh.rai@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 22:55:43 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 9/9] Android: size the Vulkan window to the canvas viewport;
 logcat trace hook

wxQt canvases are QScrollAreas whose client area (GetClientSize, which sizes the
swapchain) is the viewport inside a 1px frame.  The Vulkan window covered the
whole widget, so its surface was 2px larger than the requested swapchain and
the device waited forever for the extents to match: no frame was ever
presented.  Embed the window in the viewport instead, and route pointer and
paint events to the viewport (where wxQt handles them) and keys to the canvas.

Also add a development trace hook: masks from debug.kicad.wxtrace or a
"wxtrace" file in the app home turn on wx logging to logcat.

Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01PMkXiZQmqtvCJRtsVHJjyT
